IMPORT prelude

-- coa28-sch1.l4: Schedule 1 (Connected persons: references to an interest in shares or debentures), paragraphs 1 to 6,
-- lines 18610-18664 of ukpga-2006-46.txt (a plain-text rendering from legislation.gov.uk; not the official text).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Each paragraph is one function over plain facts; the combined question is a
-- gathering function written by hand (ruling E1, option B: a legal effect's routes gathered by hand, with every
-- route and every carve-out still a function of its own paragraph).
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING otherwise.
-- A route function that answers JUST FALSE says only "not by this paragraph"; it never says "no interest".

-- ---- paragraph 1: Introduction -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18613 | 1 (1) The provisions of this Schedule have effect for the interpretation of references in sections 254 and 255 (directors connected with or controlling a body corporate) to an interest in shares or debentures.
@ref sch 1 para 1(1) Introduction (src:18613)
GIVEN `the reference is in section 254 or 255 (directors connected with or controlling a body corporate) to an interest in shares or debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 1(1) the provisions of this Schedule govern the reference` MEANS
    IF `the reference is in section 254 or 255 (directors connected with or controlling a body corporate) to an interest in shares or debentures`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the interpretation of references in sections 254 and 255"

DECLARE `sch 1 para 1(2) kind of security` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 1(2) shares`
    `sch 1 para 1(2) debentures`
    `sch 1 para 1(2) another kind of security`

-- src:18614 | (2) The provisions are expressed in relation to shares but apply to debentures as they apply to shares.
@ref sch 1 para 1(2) Introduction (src:18614)
GIVEN security IS A `sch 1 para 1(2) kind of security`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 1(2) the provisions of this Schedule apply to the security` MEANS
    CONSIDER security
    WHEN `sch 1 para 1(2) another kind of security` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to debentures as they apply to shares"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- paragraph 2: General provisions ----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18616 | 2 (1) A reference to an interest in shares includes any interest of any kind whatsoever in shares.
@ref sch 1 para 2(1) General provisions (src:18616)
GIVEN `the person has an interest of some kind whatsoever in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 2(1) the person has an interest in the shares` MEANS
    IF `the person has an interest of some kind whatsoever in the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "A reference to an interest in shares includes any interest of any kind whatsoever in shares"

-- src:18617 | (2) Any restraints or restrictions to which the exercise of any right attached to the interest is or may be subject shall be disregarded.
@ref sch 1 para 2(2) General provisions (src:18617)
GIVEN `it is a restraint or restriction to which the exercise of any right attached to the interest is or may be subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 2(2) the restraint or restriction is disregarded` MEANS
    IF `it is a restraint or restriction to which the exercise of any right attached to the interest is or may be subject`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any restraints or restrictions to which the exercise of any right attached to the interest is or may be subject"

-- src:18618 | (3) It is immaterial that the shares in which a person has an interest are not identifiable.
@ref sch 1 para 2(3) General provisions (src:18618)
GIVEN `the shares in which the person has an interest are not identifiable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 2(3) the lack of identifiability of the shares matters to the interest` MEANS
    IF `the shares in which the person has an interest are not identifiable`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is immaterial that the shares in which a person has an interest are not identifiable"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says only that non-identifiability is immaterial

-- src:18619 | (4) Persons having a joint interest in shares are deemed each of them to have that interest.
@ref sch 1 para 2(4) General provisions (src:18619)
GIVEN `the person has a joint interest in the shares with one or more other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 2(4) the person is deemed to have the interest` MEANS
    IF `the person has a joint interest in the shares with one or more other persons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Persons having a joint interest in shares are deemed each of them to have that interest"

-- ---- paragraph 3: Rights to acquire shares ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18621 | 3 (1) A person is taken to have an interest in shares if he enters into a contract to acquire them.
@ref sch 1 para 3(1) Rights to acquire shares (src:18621)
GIVEN `the person enters into a contract to acquire the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3(1) the person is taken to have an interest in the shares by entering into a contract to acquire them` MEANS
    IF `the person enters into a contract to acquire the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is taken to have an interest in shares if he enters into a contract to acquire them" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1 in NOTES.md)

-- src:18626 | (3) Rights or obligations to subscribe for shares are not to be taken for the purposes of sub-paragraph (2) to be rights to acquire or obligations to take an interest in shares.
@ref sch 1 para 3(3) Rights to acquire shares (src:18626)
GIVEN `it is a right or obligation to subscribe for shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3(3) the right or obligation is to be taken to be a right to acquire, or an obligation to take, an interest in shares for sub-paragraph (2)` MEANS
    IF `it is a right or obligation to subscribe for shares`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights or obligations to subscribe for shares are not to be taken for the purposes of sub-paragraph (2) to be rights to acquire or obligations to take an interest in shares"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sub-paragraph speaks only of rights and obligations to subscribe

-- src:18622 | (2) A person is taken to have an interest in shares if—
-- src:18623 | (a) he has a right to call for delivery of the shares to himself or to his order, or
-- src:18624 | (b) he has a right to acquire an interest in shares or is under an obligation to take an interest in shares,
-- src:18625 | whether the right or obligation is conditional or absolute.
@ref sch 1 para 3(2) Rights to acquire shares (src:18622-18625)
GIVEN `the person has a right to call for delivery of the shares to himself or to his order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a right to acquire an interest in shares or is under an obligation to take an interest in shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that right or obligation is one to subscribe for shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3(2) the person is taken to have an interest in the shares by a right to call for delivery or a right or obligation to acquire an interest` MEANS
    IF       `the person has a right to call for delivery of the shares to himself or to his order`
         OR  (    `the person has a right to acquire an interest in shares or is under an obligation to take an interest in shares`
              AND NOT (`sch 1 para 3(3) the right or obligation is to be taken to be a right to acquire, or an obligation to take, an interest in shares for sub-paragraph (2)` `that right or obligation is one to subscribe for shares` EQUALS JUST FALSE))
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "whether the right or obligation is conditional or absolute": the condition makes no difference
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is taken to have an interest in shares if— (a) he has a right to call for delivery ..., or (b) he has a right to acquire an interest in shares or is under an obligation to take an interest in shares" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18627 | (4) A person ceases to have an interest in shares by virtue of this paragraph—
-- src:18628 | (a) on the shares being delivered to another person at his order—
-- src:18629 | (i) in fulfilment of a contract for their acquisition by him, or
-- src:18630 | (ii) in satisfaction of a right of his to call for their delivery;
-- src:18631 | (b) on a failure to deliver the shares in accordance with the terms of such a contract or on which such a right falls to be satisfied;
-- src:18632 | (c) on the lapse of his right to call for the delivery of shares.
@ref sch 1 para 3(4) Rights to acquire shares (src:18627-18632)
GIVEN `the shares are delivered to another person at his order in fulfilment of a contract for their acquisition by him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are delivered to another person at his order in satisfaction of a right of his to call for their delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a failure to deliver the shares in accordance with the terms of such a contract or on which such a right falls to be satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `his right to call for the delivery of shares lapses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3(4) the person ceases to have an interest in the shares by virtue of paragraph 3` MEANS
    IF       `the shares are delivered to another person at his order in fulfilment of a contract for their acquisition by him`
         OR  `the shares are delivered to another person at his order in satisfaction of a right of his to call for their delivery`
         OR  `there is a failure to deliver the shares in accordance with the terms of such a contract or on which such a right falls to be satisfied`
         OR  `his right to call for the delivery of shares lapses`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person ceases to have an interest in shares by virtue of this paragraph" on the events listed in (a) to (c), and the list is not closed with "only"

-- ---- paragraph 4: Right to exercise or control exercise of rights ------------------------------------------

-- src:18634 | 4 (1) A person is taken to have an interest in shares if, not being the registered holder, he is entitled—
-- src:18635 | (a) to exercise any right conferred by the holding of the shares, or
-- src:18636 | (b) to control the exercise of any such right.
@ref sch 1 para 4(1) Right to exercise or control exercise of rights (src:18634-18636)
GIVEN `the person is the registered holder of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to exercise any right conferred by the holding of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to control the exercise of any such right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 4(1) the person is taken to have an interest in the shares by an entitlement to exercise or control the exercise of a right` MEANS
    IF       NOT (`the person is the registered holder of the shares`)
         AND (`the person is entitled to exercise any right conferred by the holding of the shares` OR `the person is entitled to control the exercise of any such right`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is taken to have an interest in shares if, not being the registered holder, he is entitled— (a) to exercise any right conferred by the holding of the shares, or (b) to control the exercise of any such right" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18637 | (2) For this purpose a person is taken to be entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right conferred by the holding of shares if he—
-- src:18638 | (a) has a right (whether subject to conditions or not) the exercise of which would make him so entitled, or
-- src:18639 | (b) is under an obligation (whether or not so subject) the fulfilment of which would make him so entitled.
@ref sch 1 para 4(2) Right to exercise or control exercise of rights (src:18637-18639)
GIVEN `the person has a right (whether subject to conditions or not) the exercise of which would make him so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is under an obligation (whether or not so subject) the fulfilment of which would make him so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 4(2) the person is taken to be entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right conferred by the holding of shares` MEANS
    IF       `the person has a right (whether subject to conditions or not) the exercise of which would make him so entitled`
         OR  `the person is under an obligation (whether or not so subject) the fulfilment of which would make him so entitled`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is taken to be entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right conferred by the holding of shares if he— (a) has a right ... or (b) is under an obligation" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18640 | (3) A person is not by virtue of this paragraph taken to be interested in shares by reason only that—
-- src:18641 | (a) he has been appointed a proxy to exercise any of the rights attached to the shares, or
-- src:18642 | (b) he has been appointed by a body corporate to act as its representative at any meeting of a company or of any class of its members.
@ref sch 1 para 4(3) Right to exercise or control exercise of rights (src:18640-18642)
GIVEN `the person has been appointed a proxy to exercise any of the rights attached to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been appointed by a body corporate to act as its representative at any meeting of a company or of any class of its members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that appointment is the only reason the person would be taken to be interested under paragraph 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 4(3) the person is taken by virtue of paragraph 4 to be interested in the shares by reason only of the appointment` MEANS
    IF       (`the person has been appointed a proxy to exercise any of the rights attached to the shares` OR `the person has been appointed by a body corporate to act as its representative at any meeting of a company or of any class of its members`)
         AND `that appointment is the only reason the person would be taken to be interested under paragraph 4`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not by virtue of this paragraph taken to be interested in shares by reason only that— (a) he has been appointed a proxy ..., or (b) he has been appointed by a body corporate to act as its representative"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that"

-- ---- paragraph 5: Bodies corporate ------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- 5(2): the voting power of a second body corporate is attributed to a person who is entitled to exercise or
-- control more than one-half of the voting power at general meetings of the first.
-- src:18647 | (2) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(b) where—
-- src:18648 | (a) a person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of more than one-half of the voting power at general meetings of a body corporate, and
-- src:18649 | (b) that body corporate is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of any of the voting power at general meetings of another body corporate,
-- src:18650 | the voting power mentioned in paragraph (b) above is taken to be exercisable by that person.
@ref sch 1 para 5(2) Bodies corporate (src:18647-18650)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of more than one-half of the voting power at general meetings of a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that body corporate is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of any of the voting power at general meetings of another body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 5(2) the voting power of the other body corporate is taken to be exercisable by the person` MEANS
    IF       `the person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of more than one-half of the voting power at general meetings of a body corporate`
         AND `that body corporate is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of any of the voting power at general meetings of another body corporate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(b) where— (a) a person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of more than one-half of the voting power ..., and (b) that body corporate is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of any of the voting power ..., the voting power mentioned in paragraph (b) above is taken to be exercisable by that person" (a failed "where")

-- "more than one-half": a fraction, 0.5 itself is not more than one-half.
-- src:18646 | (b) he is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of more than one-half of the voting power at general meetings of the body corporate.
@ref sch 1 para 5(1)(b) Bodies corporate (src:18646)
GIVEN `the fraction of the voting power at general meetings that the person is entitled to exercise or control directly` IS A NUMBER
      `the fraction of the voting power at general meetings that is taken under sub-paragraph (2) to be exercisable by the person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 5(1)(b) the person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of more than one-half of the voting power at general meetings of the body corporate` MEANS
    (`the fraction of the voting power at general meetings that the person is entitled to exercise or control directly` PLUS `the fraction of the voting power at general meetings that is taken under sub-paragraph (2) to be exercisable by the person`) GREATER THAN 0.5

-- src:18644 | 5 (1) A person is taken to be interested in shares if a body corporate is interested in them and—
-- src:18645 | (a) the body corporate or its directors are accustomed to act in accordance with his directions or instructions, or
-- src:18646 | (b) he is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of more than one-half of the voting power at general meetings of the body corporate.
@ref sch 1 para 5(1) Bodies corporate (src:18644-18646)
GIVEN `a body corporate is interested in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate or its directors are accustomed to act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of more than one-half of the voting power at general meetings of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 5(1) the person is taken to be interested in the shares because a body corporate is interested in them` MEANS
    IF       `a body corporate is interested in the shares`
         AND (`the body corporate or its directors are accustomed to act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` OR `the person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of more than one-half of the voting power at general meetings of the body corporate`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is taken to be interested in shares if a body corporate is interested in them and— (a) the body corporate or its directors are accustomed to act in accordance with his directions or instructions, or (b) he is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of more than one-half of the voting power" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- ---- paragraph 6: Trusts ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18652 | 6 (1) Where an interest in shares is comprised in property held on trust, every beneficiary of the trust is taken to have an interest in shares, subject as follows.
@ref sch 1 para 6(1) Trusts (src:18652)
GIVEN `an interest in shares is comprised in property held on trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a beneficiary of the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 6(1) the beneficiary is taken to have an interest in the shares` MEANS
    IF `an interest in shares is comprised in property held on trust` AND `the person is a beneficiary of the trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "subject as follows": paragraph 6(2) to (5) are the carve-outs, applied by the gathering function below
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an interest in shares is comprised in property held on trust, every beneficiary of the trust is taken to have an interest in shares" (a failed "where")

-- src:18653 | (2) So long as a person is entitled to receive, during the lifetime of himself or another, income from trust property comprising shares, an interest in the shares in reversion or remainder or (as regards Scotland) in fee shall be disregarded.
@ref sch 1 para 6(2) Trusts (src:18653)
GIVEN `the interest is an interest in the shares in reversion or remainder or (as regards Scotland) in fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person is entitled to receive, during the lifetime of himself or another, income from trust property comprising shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 6(2) the interest in reversion, remainder or fee is disregarded` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the interest is an interest in the shares in reversion or remainder or (as regards Scotland) in fee`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an interest in the shares in reversion or remainder or (as regards Scotland) in fee"
        IF `a person is entitled to receive, during the lifetime of himself or another, income from trust property comprising shares`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "So long as a person is entitled to receive, during the lifetime of himself or another, income from trust property comprising shares"

-- src:18654 | (3) A person is treated as not interested in shares if and so long as he holds them—
-- src:18655 | (a) under the law in force in any part of the United Kingdom, as a bare trustee or as a custodian trustee, or
-- src:18656 | (b) under the law in force in Scotland, as a simple trustee.
@ref sch 1 para 6(3) Trusts (src:18654-18656)
GIVEN `the person holds the shares under the law in force in any part of the United Kingdom as a bare trustee or as a custodian trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds the shares under the law in force in Scotland as a simple trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 6(3) the person is treated as not interested in the shares` MEANS
    IF       `the person holds the shares under the law in force in any part of the United Kingdom as a bare trustee or as a custodian trustee`
         OR  `the person holds the shares under the law in force in Scotland as a simple trustee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is treated as not interested in shares if and so long as he holds them" as a bare, custodian or simple trustee

DECLARE `sch 1 para 6(4) basis of the interest` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 6(4)(a) an authorised unit trust scheme (within the meaning of section 237 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000)`
    `sch 1 para 6(4)(b) a scheme made under a charities or trustee investments enactment named in paragraph (b)`
    `sch 1 para 6(4)(c) the scheme set out in the Schedule to the Church Funds Investment Measure 1958`
    `sch 1 para 6(4) another basis`

-- src:18657 | (4) There shall be disregarded any interest of a person subsisting by virtue of—
-- src:18658 | (a) an authorised unit trust scheme (within the meaning of section 237 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8));
-- src:18659 | (b) a scheme made under section 22 or 22A of the Charities Act 1960 (c. 58), section 25 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 1964 (c. 33 (N.I.)) , section 24 or 25 of the Charities Act 1993 or section 96 or 100 of the Charities Act 2011, section 11 of the Trustee Investments Act 1961 (c. 62) or section 42 of the Administration of Justice Act 1982 (c. 53); or
-- src:18660 | (c) the scheme set out in the Schedule to the Church Funds Investment Measure 1958 (1958 No. 1).
@ref sch 1 para 6(4) Trusts (src:18657-18660)
GIVEN basis IS A `sch 1 para 6(4) basis of the interest`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 6(4) the interest is disregarded` MEANS
    CONSIDER basis
    WHEN `sch 1 para 6(4) another basis` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the list in (a) to (c) is not closed with "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `sch 1 para 6(5) interest` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 6(5)(a) an interest of the Church of Scotland General Trustees or of the Church of Scotland Trust in shares held by them`
    `sch 1 para 6(5)(b) an interest of any other person in shares held by those Trustees or that Trust otherwise than as simple trustees`
    `sch 1 para 6(5) another interest`

-- src:18661 | (5) There shall be disregarded any interest—
-- src:18662 | (a) of the Church of Scotland General Trustees or of the Church of Scotland Trust in shares held by them;
-- src:18663 | (b) of any other person in shares held by those Trustees or that Trust otherwise than as simple trustees.
@ref sch 1 para 6(5) Trusts (src:18661-18663)
GIVEN interest IS A `sch 1 para 6(5) interest`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 6(5) the interest is disregarded` MEANS
    CONSIDER interest
    WHEN `sch 1 para 6(5) another interest` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the list in (a) and (b) is not closed with "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `sch 1 para 6(5) body` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 6(5) the body incorporated by the order confirmed by the Church of Scotland (General Trustees) Order Confirmation Act 1921`
    `sch 1 para 6(5) the body incorporated by the order confirmed by the Church of Scotland Trust Order Confirmation Act 1932`
    `sch 1 para 6(5) another body`

-- src:18664 | “The Church of Scotland General Trustees” are the body incorporated by the order confirmed by the Church of Scotland (General Trustees) Order Confirmation Act 1921 (1921 c. xxv), and “the Church of Scotland Trust” is the body incorporated by the order confirmed by the Church of Scotland Trust Order Confirmation Act 1932 (1932 c. xxi).
@ref sch 1 para 6(5) Trusts (src:18664)
GIVEN body IS A `sch 1 para 6(5) body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 6(5) the body is the Church of Scotland General Trustees or the Church of Scotland Trust` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `sch 1 para 6(5) another body` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“The Church of Scotland General Trustees” are the body incorporated by the order confirmed by the Church of Scotland (General Trustees) Order Confirmation Act 1921 (1921 c. xxv), and “the Church of Scotland Trust” is the body incorporated by the order confirmed by the Church of Scotland Trust Order Confirmation Act 1932" (a quoted-term definition read as closed: marginal reading M2 in NOTES.md)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- gathering within a paragraph (ruling E1, option B): a route net of its own paragraph's carve-out ------------------

-- Paragraph 3: the routes of 3(1) and 3(2), unless the interest has ceased under 3(4).
GIVEN `the answer under sub-paragraph (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under sub-paragraph (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under sub-paragraph (4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3 the person has an interest in the shares by virtue of paragraph 3` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer under sub-paragraph (4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person ceases to have an interest in shares by virtue of this paragraph" on the events in (4)(a) to (c)
        IF `the answer under sub-paragraph (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer under sub-paragraph (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the answer under sub-paragraph (1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the answer under sub-paragraph (2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): neither sub-paragraph (1) nor (2) holds (marginal reading M1 in NOTES.md)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a sub-paragraph's answer is not given

-- Paragraph 4: the route of 4(1), unless the person is interested by reason only of a proxy or representative appointment.
GIVEN `the answer under sub-paragraph (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under sub-paragraph (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 4 the person has an interest in the shares by virtue of paragraph 4` MEANS
    IF `the answer under sub-paragraph (3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not by virtue of this paragraph taken to be interested in shares by reason only that" he is a proxy or a corporate representative
    ELSE `the answer under sub-paragraph (1)`

-- Paragraph 6: the beneficiary's interest of 6(1), unless 6(2) disregards it.
GIVEN `the answer under sub-paragraph (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under sub-paragraph (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 6 the beneficiary has an interest in the shares by virtue of paragraph 6` MEANS
    IF `the answer under sub-paragraph (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an interest in the shares in reversion or remainder or (as regards Scotland) in fee shall be disregarded"
    ELSE `the answer under sub-paragraph (1)`

-- ---- the gathering function (ruling E1, option B) ---------------------------------------------------------

-- Each route is the answer of one paragraph (2(1), 3(1), 3(2), 4(1), 5(1), 6(1)), already netted by that
-- paragraph's own carve-out (3(4), 4(3), 6(2)). The exclusions are the answers of 6(3), 6(4) and 6(5).
-- This function states no rule of its own: it only says "an exclusion that holds wins; otherwise one route is enough".
GIVEN routes IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
      exclusions IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 paras 2 to 6 the person has an interest in the shares or debentures for sections 254 and 255` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN r YIELD r EQUALS JUST TRUE) exclusions
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is treated as not interested in shares if and so long as he holds them" / "There shall be disregarded any interest" (paragraph 6(3) to (5))
        IF any (GIVEN r YIELD r EQUALS JUST TRUE) routes
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "A reference to an interest in shares includes any interest of any kind whatsoever", so no route found is not "no interest"
